<%# Locals: `user`; `size:` one of lg md row nav sm (default md); `variant:` :photo
     (default) or :tile; `class:` extra utilities.

     `size:` IS the pixel box — lg 96 · md 44 · row 40 · nav 36 · sm 32. A `w-*` passed
     through `class:` does not override that, it competes with it, and the winner is
     whichever class the Tailwind bundle emits later (numeric order), not the caller's
     intent: `class: "w-8"` against `size: :lg` loses. Pass margins and other
     layout-neutral utilities through `class:`; to change the box, change `size:`.

     `variant:` is the SHAPE and is ORTHOGONAL to `size:` (Hoojah 2026, redesign Phase
     0 Task 0.2) — a tile still needs a size, so it is its own local rather than a
     sixth AVATAR_SIZES key. `:photo` (default) shows the user's round photo, falling
     back to initials on the gradient tile when there isn't one — same as before this
     local existed. `:tile` is the gradient-initials TREATMENT itself
     (docs/design-system/components/core/Avatar.jsx): it renders initials on
     `.avatar-tile` even for a user who has a photo, for surfaces (navbar, feed cards)
     that want the tile look on purpose, not merely as a fallback.

     Deliberately NOT a Rails strict-locals signature: one of the locals is `class`, which
     cannot be a Ruby parameter name, so the whole signature is unavailable to this partial.

     A user's round photo, or their initials on the gradient tile when there isn't one
     (or when `variant: :tile` asks for the tile outright).

     The fallback is not decoration. `photo` is nullable and `image_tag nil` raises,
     so every `image_tag user.photo` in the app is a 500 waiting for a user without a
     photo — see docs/design-system/components/core/Avatar.jsx, which this mirrors.

     Three details that look cosmetic and are not:

     - Both branches are block-level (`block` / `flex`, never `inline-flex`). An inline
       box sits on a line box and collects descender leading that the `block` img does
       not, so a photoless user would shift the row by a few px — and `.inline-flex`
       follows `.hidden` in the bundle, so `class: "hidden lg:block"` would hide the
       photo branch while leaving the initials visible.
     - `role="img"` on the fallback. ARIA ignores an author-supplied `aria-label` on a
       bare `<span>` (role=generic), which is exactly the case where a screen reader
       reads out the raw letters "MZ" instead of the name.
     - The same name on both branches, as in Avatar.jsx. Announcing one person two
       different ways depending on whether they uploaded a photo is a bug; the handle
       is not always adjacent either (see shared/_navbar).
%><% tile = local_assigns[:variant] == :tile %>
<% avatar_url = tile ? nil : ds_avatar_url(user) %>
<% tile ||= avatar_url.blank? %>
<% box = "#{ds_avatar_classes(size: local_assigns[:size], variant: (tile ? :tile : :photo))} shrink-0 #{local_assigns[:class]}".squish %>
<% if tile %>
  <span role="img" aria-label="<%= user.full_name %>"
        class="<%= box %> flex items-center justify-center text-white font-medium tracking-wide"><%= ds_initials(user.full_name) %></span>
<% else %>
  <%= image_tag avatar_url, alt: user.full_name, class: "#{box} block object-cover" %>
<% end %>
